## Original Content
Archeologists are confronting an “unfathomable” loss as border wall construction is set to cut across ranches that are home to unique historical sites, many of which haven’t been fully studied.

## Summary
Border wall construction in the US threatens to destroy or damage historical sites on private lands, posing an 'unfathomable' loss of up to 6,000 years of history, much of which remains unstudied. Archeologists are racing against time as the project advances across ranches. The destruction could erase invaluable cultural and archaeological records.

## Key Points
- Border wall construction impacts private lands with historical sites
- Sites span up to 6,000 years of history, largely unstudied
- Archeologists face 'unfathomable' loss due to the project's progression


